config LICHEN_UX
	bool "LICHEN device UX (spec 19)"
	depends on LICHEN
	default y
	help
	  Device UX components from spec/19-device-ux.md. Compiles the pure,
	  host-testable engines (LED timing, etc.); GPIO/display backends are
	  individually selectable.

config LICHEN_UX_LED
	bool "Spec 19 §10 LED status language (led0 blink engine)"
	depends on LICHEN_UX
	default y
	help
	  Drive the device status LED with the fixed 6-state blink table from
	  spec 19 §10 (joined-idle off, joining, message-waiting, SOS, hold,
	  fault). Selects the GPIO backend that drives led0 via the HAL.
	  Boards set CONFIG_LICHEN_HAS_LEDS (which BUILD_ASSERTs an led0 alias);
	  targets with no LED (hal_led_get fails) degrade to a quiet no-op and
	  the driver does not schedule any periodic work.

config LICHEN_UX_BUTTON
	bool "Spec 19 §4/§8/§9 button interaction grammar (screen ring + SOS + reset)"
	depends on LICHEN_UX
	depends on LICHEN_UX_LED
	default y
	help
	  Drive the user button with the universal interaction grammar from
	  spec 19 §4: short-press advances the screen ring, hold >=2s arms
	  SOS (single-button hardware, §8), hold >=5s opens the guarded
	  factory-reset path (§9), with mandatory hold feedback within 500 ms
	  (the H-tier LED switches to the 4 Hz hold pattern, §10). The pure
	  grammar engine is always compiled; this selects the GPIO backend
	  that reads the user button via the HAL. Targets with no button
	  (hal_button_get fails) degrade to a quiet no-op.
